Feature: promoted native known-stops and the one_byte oracle — folded from the retired native_union / one_byte projects (0.3.1 consolidation)

  # (native_union_scalar) THE NATIVE BACKEND'S NULL-UNION STOP, PROMOTED. Owner ruling 2026-07-28:
  # "trocar a asserção para esperar por falha honesta". CLOSED (cargo/0.3.1.0-null-adopt): `probe()`
  # returns 42 on BOTH routes. What closed it is narrow — `lower_cast` unconditionally asked
  # `prim_kind_of` for its cast's own type, which has no single machine class for a `Variant`; a
  # `Variant`-targeted cast (the synthetic widening node the const inliner wraps a scalar-const
  # reference in) now routes through `lower_value_into_type`. The general `.32` UnionRepr porting is
  # NOT claimed done — only this shape (a numeric null-union reached through the const-inliner's widen)
  # is verified. It is a MEMBER now that it lowers: one build, asserting the value the C route always
  # produced (40 present + 2 absent-fallback = 42).
  Scenario: native_union_scalar (own-native — a numeric null-union reached through the const-inliner's widen now lowers)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario native_union_scalar: ok"

  # (native_union_nested) CLOSED — 0.3.1.0 degrau 25. A null-union struct nested INSIDE another
  # null-union field, the shape the native placement-coercion stop was first measured on. Every
  # own-backend placement coerces its value into the slot's DECLARED type (`lower_value_into_type`)
  # except two that had no declared type — a struct-literal field and a call argument;
  # `collect_field_decls` and `callee_param_types` are what those placements now read. Both levels
  # present (30), inner `null` (fallback 5), outer `null` (fallback 7) sum to 42, so a wrapper written
  # at either level with the wrong tag shows up as a WRONG SUM, not a stop.
  Scenario: native_union_nested (own-native — a null-union field nested inside a null-union field round-trips both levels)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario native_union_nested: ok"

  # (generic_fn_constructs_generic) THE fix/generic-stamping rung. A generic FREE FUNCTION
  # (`gfc_wrap<T>`) constructs a generic TYPE (`GfcBox<T>`) from its own still-abstract type-param.
  # Before the fix the construction node kept the phantom `GfcBox__g__T` and the checker aborted
  # ("internal: generic instance `GfcBox__g__T` was not stamped"); the monomorph pass now re-mangles
  # the phantom through the bound `T` (`subst_instance_name`) so `gfc_wrap<i64>`/`gfc_wrap<u8>` each
  # build their own concrete stamp. The value 42 = 40 (i64 instance) + 2 (u8 instance) + two zero seeds.
  Scenario: generic_fn_constructs_generic (own-native — a generic fn constructs a generic type from its own type-param)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario generic_fn_constructs_generic: ok"

  # (n112_region_lifetime_selfappend_in_virtual_main) THE N112 region-lifetime regression. A
  # by-address aggregate (`n112::Item`) whose variant `content` holds a FAT-element `[]str` payload is
  # self-appended into a `[]Item` inside a TOP-LEVEL `main.tks` loop, then read back (`n112::readback`).
  # A virtual-main opens no frame region, so the accumulator's base region is the loop's OWN
  # per-iteration body; `enter_self_append_region`'s fallback used to bracket the grow + element box
  # (`tk_slice_elem_box`) to `region_stack[0]` — that per-iteration region — which `close_loop_body`
  # reclaims each turn, dangling every by-address element and faulting the read-back (the self-hosted
  # `assemble_sel` gen2==gen3 crash; probe `examples/probes/n112_assemble_sel_crash`). The fallback now
  # routes a virtual-main top-level accumulator's growth to the ROOT (`enter_self_append_fallback`), so
  # the fold reaches its 108 (72 trailing-str + 24 Func-case + 12 TypeDecl-case). A REAL function is
  # unaffected: its `region_stack[0]` is a durable frame, not a loop body.
  Scenario: n112_region_lifetime_selfappend_in_virtual_main (own-native — a fat-element-payload aggregate self-appended in a virtual-main loop survives the region drop)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario n112_region_lifetime_selfappend_in_virtual_main: ok"

  # (one_byte_native) `teko::one_byte(byte): str` existed in the checker and the runtime mirror but
  # was NOT lowered natively: `call_symbol` found no symbol and returned `unresolved_builtin_stop`.
  # The exit sums SIX disjoint weights (3, 12, 16, 32, 64, 128 = 255), one per call shape: the minimal
  # call, the escape-accumulation of `json.tks:218-225`, the UTF-8 pair of `json.tks:296`, a byte from
  # a slice index, two live results at once, and the NUL byte. No partial sum reaches 255, so a shape
  # that falls moves the number and names itself. The C-route oracle for the same 255 rides as
  # `cases/one_byte_c.tks` (env C — the shared project build's config is fixed by the first scenario's
  # env, so the two routes cannot share one build).
  Scenario: one_byte_native (own-native — the six call shapes of `one_byte` each produce their own byte and length)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario one_byte_native: ok"

  # (one_byte_c) the C route of the `one_byte` regressor, the ORACLE of the value the native side
  # asserts. `Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]` fixes a STANDALONE build (its own synthesized manifest),
  # so it never shares the native member build above. The same program, the same 255: the C route
  # reaches it by `tk_one_byte` (a `tk_str` struct return by value) and the native route by
  # `tk_one_byte_len` (pointer in the result register, length through the hidden out-slot) — two
  # independent realizations that must agree on the number.
  Scenario: one_byte_c (C route — the same 255 the native member asserts, through tk_one_byte)
    Given source = "cases/one_byte_c.tks"
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "255"

  # (native_iface_fat) A KNOWN-STOP still open: a fat (`str`) result arriving through INTERFACE
  # DISPATCH. The arm calls `v.speak()` — a VIRTUAL dispatch whose result is `str` — and
  # `lower_call_fat`'s own narrower stop refuses a fat result through a vtable. Nothing declares a loose
  # `null`; both bindings are annotated `Animal_sbmd | null` and receive what that type accepts, so the
  # stop is the backend's, not a bad fixture. It rides as a `Given source` compile-fail (it aborts the
  # build and cannot be a member of the successful shared build). PROMOTE to a member (`When built and
  # run` / value 42) the day the fat interface-dispatch result lands. (Four bulk scenarios hit this
  # exact stop while being triaged — `class_base_binding`, `class_inheritance`,
  # `class_invariant_construction`, `class_upcast` — reported, not re-pinned: identical diagnostic.)
  Scenario: native_iface_fat (own-native — a str-returning virtual method called through its base stops honestly)
    Given source = "cases/native_iface_fat.tks"
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "fat-pointer interface-dispatch result not yet lowered"

